      "page_idx": 17,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "header",
          "bbox": [
            0.551,
            0.069,
            0.815,
            0.087
          ],
          "content": "Exploring Algebraic Identities"
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "bbox": [
            0.855,
            0.069,
            0.883,
            0.084
          ],
          "content": "85"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.148,
            0.107,
            0.825,
            0.18
          ],
          "content": "Thus $( x - y ) ( x ^ { 2 } + x y + y ^ { 2 } ) = x ^ { 3 } - y ^ { 3 }$ . This is also an identity! Verify this for yourself by choosing different values of x and y. Predict what $( x + y ) ( x ^ { 2 } - x y + y ^ { 2 } )$ will be."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.132,
            0.204,
            0.399,
            0.227
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Think and Reflect"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.128,
            0.242,
            0.605,
            0.267
          ],
          "content": "We already know that $x^{2}-y^{2}=(x-y)(x+y)$ ."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.129,
            0.272,
            0.748,
            0.301
          ],
          "content": "Further, we have verified that $x^{3}-y^{3}=(x-y)\\left(x^{2}+xy+y^{2}\\right)$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.129,
            0.303,
            0.698,
            0.322
          ],
          "content": "Observe that $X - y$ is a common factor of $X ^ { 2 }   -   y ^ { 2 }$ and $X ^ { 3 }   -   y ^ { 3 } .$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.129,
            0.329,
            0.558,
            0.349
          ],
          "content": "Do you think x – y is also a factor of $X ^ { 4 }   -   y ^ { 4 } ?$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.13,
            0.355,
            0.585,
            0.375
          ],
          "content": "Note that $X ^ { 4 } - y ^ { 4 } = ( X ^ { 2 } ) ^ { 2 } - ( y ^ { 2 } ) ^ { 2 } = ( X ^ { 2 } - y ^ { 2 } ) \\; ( X ^ { 2 } + y ^ { 2 } ) .$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.13,
            0.382,
            0.552,
            0.401
          ],
          "content": "Can you see how x – y is a factor of $X ^ { 4 }   -   y ^ { 4 } ?$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.13,
            0.407,
            0.673,
            0.427
          ],
          "content": "How about $X ^ { 5 }   -   y ^ { 5 } ?$ Does this also have $x - y$ as a factor?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.449,
            0.881,
            0.47
          ],
          "content": "Exploring further, let us multiply $(x + y + z)$ and $(x^{2}+y^{2}+z^{2}-xy-xz-yz)$"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.473,
            0.822,
            0.643
          ],
          "content": "\\begin{aligned} &\\left( (x + y + z)\\left( x^{2} + y^{2} + z^{2} - xy - xz^{2} - yz \\right) \\right. \\\\&= \\left. \\left( x^{3} + xy^{2} + xz^{2} - x^{2}y - xz^{2}z - yz \\right) + \\left( x^{2}y + y^{3} + yz^{2} - xy^{2} - xyz - y^{2}z \\right) \\right. \\\\&\\quad + \\left. \\left( x^{2}z + y^{2}z + z^{3} - xyz - xz^{2} - yz^{2} \\right) \\right. \\\\&= \\left. \\left( x^{3} + xy^{2} + xz^{2} - x^{2}y - xz^{2}z - xyz \\right) + \\left( x^{2}y + y^{3} + yz^{2} - xy^{2} - xyz - y^{2}z \\right) \\right. \\\\&\\quad + \\left. \\left( x^{2}z + y^{2}z^{2} + z^{3} - xyz - xz^{2} - yz^{2} \\right) \\right. \\\\&= x^{3} + y^{3} + z^{3} - 3xyz. \\\\&\\left. \\left( \\mathrm{So}, (x + y + z)\\left( x^{2} + y^{2} + z^{2} - xy - xz - yz \\right) = x^{3} + y^{3} + z^{3} - 3xyz. \\right. \\right.\\end{aligned}",
          "image_source": "images/page_17_equation_12.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.647,
            0.872,
            0.668
          ],
          "content": "This is yet another identity. Let us explore some of its applications."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.112,
            0.673,
            0.885,
            0.731
          ],
          "content": "**Example 15:** The sum of three numbers is 10 and their product is 25. The sum of their squares is 38. Try to use the previous identity to find the sum of the cubes of these three numbers."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.112,
            0.731,
            0.884,
            0.771
          ],
          "content": "Let the three numbers be x, y and $Z ,$ respectively. According to the problem $x \\mp y \\mp z = 10, \\quad xyz = 25$ and $x ^ { 2 } + y ^ { 2 } + { \\bar { z ^ { 2 } } } = 3 8$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.77,
            0.447,
            0.789
          ],
          "content": "Substituting in the identity"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.148,
            0.795,
            0.818,
            0.815
          ],
          "content": "( x + y + z ) ( x ^ { 2 } + y ^ { 2 } + z ^ { 2 } - x y - x z - y z ) = x ^ { 3 } + y ^ { 3 } + z ^ { 3 } - 3 x y z , \\mathrm { w e ~ g e t }",
          "image_source": "images/page_17_equation_17.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.819,
            0.611,
            0.84
          ],
          "content": "(10) $( 3 8 - x y - x z - y z ) = x ^ { 3 } + y ^ { 3 } + z ^ { 3 } - 3 \\; ( 2 5 ) .$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.844,
            0.883,
            0.866
          ],
          "content": "Thus, $x^{3}+y^{3}+z^{3}=380-10\\left ( xy+xz+yz \\right ) +75=455-10\\left ( xy+xz+yz \\right ) .$"
        }
      ]
    }
